{{Shortcut|Template:UWI}}{{Documentation/Header}}
This template provides a simple, customizable inline wrapper for inserting Utaite Wiki's custom icons into your wikitext. It uses relative scaling (<code>em</code>), meaning the icons will naturally match the text size of their surrounding container unless overridden. It also supports dynamic animations and transformations.
== Syntax ==
{{T|UWI|v1=icon=icon_name|v2=class=utility_classes|v3=color=color|v4=size=custom_size|v5=animation-duration=time|v6=animation-iteration-count=number|v7=rotate-angle=angle}}

== Examples ==

=== Basic Sizing & Styling ===
Standard usage (inherits text size):
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nicovideo|p2=color=#68ecfa|_Y_=1}}

Using predefined sizing classes (<code>uw-2xs</code>, <code>uw-xs</code>, <code>uw-sm</code>, <code>uw-lg</code>, <code>uw-xl</code>, <code>uw-2xl</code>):
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nagareboshi|p2=class=uw-2xl|_Y_=1}}

Using a custom inline size (overrides predefined classes):
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nagareboshi|p2=size=3rem|p3=color=#ffcc00|_Y_=1}}

=== Animations ===
Standard continuous spin (great for loading states):
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nicovideo|p2=class=uw-spin|p3=color=#999|_Y_=1}}

A fast, pulsing heartbeat effect using custom duration:
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nagareboshi|p2=class=uw-beat|p3=color=#ff5555|p4=animation-duration=0.5s|_Y_=1}}

A slow bounce that only loops exactly 3 times before stopping:
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nagareboshi|p2=class=uw-bounce|p3=animation-duration=2s|p4=animation-iteration-count=3|_Y_=1}}

=== Transformations ===
Flipping an icon horizontally:
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nicovideo|p2=class=uw-flip-horizontal|_Y_=1}}

Applying a precise, custom rotation (e.g., tilting 45 degrees):
{{T|UWI|p1=icon=nagareboshi|p2=class=uw-rotate-by|p3=rotate-angle=45deg|_Y_=1}}

